## f2f15d832fb1

**Reproduced defect:** every advertised exact structural override in the replay is accepted but ignored, and the generator has no `self_check` to enforce task invariants.

Replay `seed=321`, `sample_index=0`, `difficulty=medium` with no overrides and with `grid_h=9`, `grid_w=18`, `n_objects=1`, `blob_size=8`, `density=sparse`. Both outputs have SHA-256 `853d818bab443ef8d60728453dfec13a071ae43d3df32d0951a734ebe9a76d6f` and are byte-identical. The requested 9×18 grid with one size-eight object is instead 11×14 with two nonzero components of sizes six and four. Full grids and counts are retained in `checks/audit/f2f15d832fb1/repro.json`.

Independent gates corroborate the defect:

- lint fails for missing `RULE_HASH` and missing `self_check` (`checks/audit/f2f15d832fb1-lint/checks/f2f15d832fb1_audit_lint.log`);
- the mandatory self-check stage fails explicitly (`checks/audit/f2f15d832fb1-selfcheck/checks/f2f15d832fb1_audit_selfcheck.log`);
- strict defect lint finds dead helpful textures, permissive scalar handling, unlawful negative textures, and canonical object-size drift (canonical median maximum object size 10 vs generated range 4–7) (`checks/audit/f2f15d832fb1-defect_lint/checks/f2f15d832fb1_audit_defect_lint.log`);
- profile floor has only 8/60 exact hits, 27/60 envelope hits, zero required exact support in the hard band, and no callable `self_check` (`checks/audit/f2f15d832fb1-profile_floor/checks/f2f15d832fb1_audit_profile_floor.log`);
- semantic audit fails because no semantic contract exists (`checks/audit/f2f15d832fb1/checks/f2f15d832fb1_audit_semantic_gate.log`).

**Impact:** callers cannot rely on the documented intervention contract, and malformed or off-rule samples have no task-local executable rejection path. No repair was made because this was an audit-only target.
